       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the safe maximum, so I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Each dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3200 mg/day.\n\nAt this dose the patient has a much higher risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and other NSAID toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1600 mg/day). This is a common anti-inflammatory dose, and 1600 mg may have been meant as the daily total.\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3200 mg/day). This is the maximum.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do mean 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a reason I can put in the order note. In that case I'd also recommend checking with pharmacy before it's dispensed."
